 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! A GAMESS Google Group response (from a related but different thread)          
 INPUT CARD>! suggested trying the PCseg family (Jensen's Polarization Consistent           
 INPUT CARD>! segmented basis sets) as an alternative to cc-pVTZ/def2-TZVPP-style           
 INPUT CARD>! bases, specifically raising the possibility that the CONSTRUCTION of          
 INPUT CARD>! those basis families could itself be contributing to linear-dependence-       
 INPUT CARD>! type problems, and that a newer basis family might behave better.             
 INPUT CARD>! PCseg-2 is roughly equivalent in quality to cc-pVTZ (~TZ2P).                  
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! This is a genuinely attractive test for two independent reasons:              
 INPUT CARD>! 1. It directly tests the forum's scientific hypothesis (does a                
 INPUT CARD>!    differently-constructed triple-zeta-quality basis show the same            
 INPUT CARD>!    instability at this geometry?).                                            
